{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2288 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "6941cf9c270c5d4b61964e28cc0364c3c0a208bb9df9dcf758032404eee57ee8" :edb/db-before-t 2287 :edb/db-after-t 2288 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535600 50 #inst "2026-10-09T03:22:35.380Z" 13194139535600 true] [17592186096625 1020 #edb/ref 17592186356973 13194139535600 true] [17592186096626 1020 #edb/ref 17592186356980 13194139535600 true] [17592186356973 1017 #edb/ref 17592186356974 13194139535600 true] [17592186356973 1089 "q-115643" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356973 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535600 true] [17592186356973 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/assets/1f6330a6e9bc0e48326982c7b7509f3e2257de994c5736c813ede93a07491e70.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356973 1113 #uuid "77c89899-e75a-59ab-bd2e-ad4bcdbad022" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356973 1145 "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,-3)$ and passes through the point $(3,0).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(0,-3),$ we substitute $h=0$ and $k=-3$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4px.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(3,0),$ so we can substitute $x=3$ and $y=0$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4px \\\\ (0+3)^{2} & =4p(3) \\\\ 9 & =12p \\\\ p & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4px \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =4(\\frac{3}{4})x \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=\\frac{3}{4}$ is positive." 13194139535600 true] [17592186356974 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356975 13194139535600 true] [17592186356974 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356976 13194139535600 true] [17592186356974 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356977 13194139535600 true] [17592186356974 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356978 13194139535600 true] [17592186356974 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356979 13194139535600 true] [17592186356974 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535600 true] [17592186356974 1041 "selection" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356974 1104 #edb/ref 17592186356976 13194139535600 true] [17592186356974 1110 #uuid "07b63f6e-8114-5be1-acc3-057df4a03f76" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356975 1034 "(y+3)^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}x" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356975 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535600 true] [17592186356975 1111 #uuid "69a0dbc2-368b-50cf-8181-53aaf11d8756" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356976 1034 "(y+3)^{2}=3x" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356976 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535600 true] [17592186356976 1111 #uuid "5cc6ebe0-056c-5db3-aa4d-00da2d08a862" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356977 1034 "{y}^{2}=3(x+3)" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356977 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535600 true] [17592186356977 1111 #uuid "a99a99b6-7751-5bd4-87be-086d24316fd0" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356978 1034 "(x+3)^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}y" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356978 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535600 true] [17592186356978 1111 #uuid "36fa5fed-3280-56d5-b4a5-e6d52d91da01" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356979 1034 "(x-3)^{2}=3y" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356979 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535600 true] [17592186356979 1111 #uuid "88381818-e2b1-51c9-9e9e-465ad7fc25b1" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356980 1017 #edb/ref 17592186356981 13194139535600 true] [17592186356980 1089 "q-115646" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356980 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535600 true] [17592186356980 1100 "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(1,-3)$ and passes through the point $(3,0).$" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356980 1113 #uuid "6abb456a-0967-521f-9352-1d7bccf90856" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356980 1145 "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(1,-3),$ we substitute $h=1$ and $k=-3$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4p(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(3,0),$ so we can substitute $x=3$ and $y=0$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4p(x-1) \\\\ (0+3)^{2} & =4p(3-1) \\\\ 9 & =8p \\\\ p & =\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4p(x-1) \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =4(\\frac{9}{8})(x-1) \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =\\frac{9}{2}(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356981 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356982 13194139535600 true] [17592186356981 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356983 13194139535600 true] [17592186356981 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356984 13194139535600 true] [17592186356981 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356985 13194139535600 true] [17592186356981 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356986 13194139535600 true] [17592186356981 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535600 true] [17592186356981 1041 "selection" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356981 1104 #edb/ref 17592186356984 13194139535600 true] [17592186356981 1110 #uuid "1e5a7402-d90a-5909-85eb-d6a5f0698f31" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356982 1034 "(y-3)^{2}=\\frac{9}{2}(x+1)" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356982 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535600 true] [17592186356982 1111 #uuid "42d05c86-a4fd-5d27-a816-2fb3d493a1c9" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356983 1034 "(y+3)^{2}=36(x-1)" 13194139535600 true] [17592186356983 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535600 true] [1759218635